! mcp_bootstrap_p314.strap -- MCP printed page 314: the tail of the
! disk-arc read set-up begun on p.313 (V-I/LC/LR, CW DISK, M+1 CLUK, the
! TI of one arc), the copy loop C T, the bookkeeping to X RETN and the
! MCP D RET return, C BUFT / C FAST (form C FOT, ALPHA = BETA + arc),
! the C NARK re-entry to C RODE and C NOLOC; lines 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.65, read at 400 dpi, doubtful glyphs
! at 900 dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD
! ID SB000128  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 314"; the heading row's
! LOCATION field is 234021, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines, then blank paper.  Every line number prints a "*"
! after it.  No remark cards, no TAIL card.  Located rows run contiguous
! from 234021.40 (line 1) to 234061.40 (line 50, a half-word B; next
! location 234062.00).  "*" after the LOCATION on lines 13, 32 and 48.
!   lines 39-42  B,D MCP and its calling sequence ,D LOCS / ,PROSA / ,0,
!                the same sequence p.312 lines 17-20 print.
! JOIN.  p.313 (b8decks) ends at 234021.00, a half-word SVA, next
! location 234021.40: this page's line 1 continues it.  p.315 should open
! at 234062.00.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * "CW CISK" (line 4) and "CWCISK" (line 6) = CWDISK: D with its stem
!     worn; same TI shape as p.313 line 36 TI,1,CWDCRD,CWRD.  Name used
!     only here; value from the binary (234217.00).
!   * "B, C MCP" (line 25) = B,DMCP: D worn, as on p.312 line 17; line 39
!     prints the same card with the stem whole; 000040.10 = DMCP 32.0.
!   * ", S D RET" (line 26) = SDRET, landed stand-in value 33.0 (p.105).
!   * "C NOLOC" (lines 35, 49): both O's print CLOSED at 900 dpi; the last
!     glyph is a real open C.  "C FOT" (lines 28, 30, 31): O closed, and
!     C22-6728 prints CFOT.  XRETN is a C22-6728 spelling.
!   * "X LC ALF" (line 37): the glyph after L is open round; nothing
!     closes it to O, no deck or C22-6728 names the symbol: written as
!     the ink, XLCALF.
!   * "M+1(BU,18)" (line 5): the glyph after "+" has the 1's flag and base
!     (as the 1 of "18" beside it), not the serif I of "SIC": the op is
!     M+1 (add one to memory).
!   * LINE 5'S LAST BYTE PRINTS "BC" AND IS B0: the glyph after B is the
!     same open round this row prints in its octal fields (234402.CC);
!     the statement prints no second-operand index, so the low nibble
!     can only be 0 (brief lesson 6; p.197 / p.313 "AC" = A0 cases).
!   * "1.C" (line 18), "C.0" (line 1), "C.0($7)" / "C.0($8)" (line 11),
!     ", C" (line 42): open round glyphs read as digit 0 (000000.00 80 on
!     line 42, as p.312 line 20).
!   * octal / hex fields with an open round read 0 ("0D", "80", "C0" =
!     00, "A0", "F0", "D0", "50", "10").
!   * names spaced by the drum (CW DISK, C GAMMA, C DELTA, C N, C N PRIM,
!     C LR, S D RET, C BUFT, C FOT, C FAST, C BETA, C ALPHA, C NOLOC,
!     X LC ALF, D LOCS, C PRERD, C NARK, C RODE, C NOLOC, CHK PAR, C T)
!     written closed up.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  SB000128 .. SB000168.  p.313 ends at SB000126: NO
! SB000127 is printed on either page.  Shared serials: lines 2-3
! (SB000129), 14-16 (SB000140, three lines), 19-20 (SB000143), 22-23
! (SB000145), 27-28 (SB000149), 29-30 (SB000150), 47-48 (SB000167),
! 49-50 (SB000168).  Line 17's serial prints a mark over its S.
!
! EXTERNALS.  Values for symbols defined on pages not landed come from
! this page's binary or the b8decks stand-ins (each comment says which).

